00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:34.792
(Jean laughs)

00:01:34.792 --> 00:01:35.625
- Oh, my gosh, really?

00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:36.458
- [Audience Members] Aww.

00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:37.291
- [Jean] Yeah.

00:01:37.291 --> 00:01:38.229
I don't mean we moved in
together the next day,

00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:39.062
I don't mean that.

00:01:39.062 --> 00:01:39.895
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:39.895 --> 00:01:40.728
(audience laughs)

00:01:40.728 --> 00:01:41.561
I don't mean that.

00:01:41.561 --> 00:01:42.394
- This is happening.

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:43.580
- Yeah, no, and he invited me

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:44.730
to come and see a play that he was doing.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.260
Of course I went 17 times.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.093
- [Kelly] Aww.

00:01:47.093 --> 00:01:47.926
- And then, you know,

00:01:47.926 --> 00:01:49.030
we lived about 15 minutes apart

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.240
but we would talk every night on the phone

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.463
for about two hours.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.630
- I love that!

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.330
That's rare to find that, wow!

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:57.650
But speaking of family,

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.887
so we both did that show,

00:01:58.887 --> 00:02:00.140
"Who Do You Think You Are?"

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:00.973
- Yes.

00:02:00.973 --> 00:02:04.720
- I loved it, but I heard
yours was really rad.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.010
What was the coolest
thing that you found out?

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:09.460
- Well, my cousin, Darlene,

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.660
on my mom's side of the family,

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.570
has researched my mother's
maternal side of the family

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.403
to death.

00:02:14.403 --> 00:02:15.331
So I thought,

00:02:15.331 --> 00:02:17.330
how could they have found
something interesting enough

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:18.800
to make an episode about?

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:19.635
- Yeah. They did.

00:02:19.635 --> 00:02:21.120
- You know, it's a reality show,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.130
that Darlene didn't
already dig up, you know?

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.080
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.150
- And they went all the way back

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.510
to my eight times great-grandmother.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.800
She had an unfortunate name.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.723
Her first name was Dorcas
and her last name was Hoar.

00:02:32.723 --> 00:02:34.345
(audience laughs)

00:02:34.345 --> 00:02:36.928
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.440
- Like, how do you spell Hoar?

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.080
- Yeah, well it was spelled H-O-A-R,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.510
but in some of the documents,

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.370
one of the documents I read,

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:51.270
I actually got to hold original
documents from the 1600s.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.103
- [Kelly] What?

00:02:52.103 --> 00:02:54.270
- And they wrote it

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.610
as if they thought that
was her profession.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.312
Dorcas, comma, Hoar.

00:02:57.312 --> 00:02:59.240
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:03.050
- But no, she was accused
of witchcraft in 1692

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.800
in Salem, Massachusetts.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.990
She lived in Beverly,
which is right next door.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:11.630
And she was convicted
and sentenced to hang.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:15.280
And, she missed being hanged by one day.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.840
She confessed and that
bought her some time.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.039
And in that time,

00:03:20.039 --> 00:03:24.048
the public kinda lost its
taste for these hangings.

00:03:24.048 --> 00:03:24.910
And so they thought,

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.828
maybe we're killing some innocent people,

00:03:26.828 --> 00:03:28.585
I don't know if we should be doing this.

00:03:28.585 --> 00:03:29.418
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:29.418 --> 00:03:31.483
- But I called my husband
that night and I said,

00:03:31.483 --> 00:03:32.760
"You're not gonna believe it.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.580
You're not gonna believe
what they found out."

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:36.413
And I told him,

00:03:36.413 --> 00:03:38.327
and there was this long pause and he said,

00:03:38.327 --> 00:03:40.281
"Well, that explains a lot."

00:03:40.281 --> 00:03:41.114
(Kelly cracks up)

00:03:41.114 --> 00:03:42.012
(audience laughs)

00:03:42.012 --> 00:03:43.750
- I totally would've gone
through a whole thing like,

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.310
well, I'm totally a witch.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:46.593
I would've been so excited about it.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.864
- Are you a good witch?

00:03:47.864 --> 00:03:48.697
Or a bad witch?

00:03:48.697 --> 00:03:50.373
- [Kelly] I would've been a good witch.

00:03:50.373 --> 00:03:51.364
I'd have used my power for good.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.197
(audience applauding)

00:03:52.197 --> 00:03:53.323
So that was look at her show, "Hacks."

00:03:53.323 --> 00:03:55.900
Season Two is on HBO Max now.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.180
It's such an incredible show,

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.557
so congrats on all the love for "Hacks."

00:03:59.557 --> 00:04:00.390
"Hacks" is so good.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.393
- Oh, thank you. Thank you.

00:04:01.393 --> 00:04:02.226
(audience cheers)

00:04:02.226 --> 00:04:07.050
- Honestly, I started watching
it because I love you.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.120
I started watching it just
'cause I'm a huge fan of yours.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.000
And then, it's such a good show.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:11.833
- Yeah.

00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:12.800
- It's funny, it's intense,

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.500
it can be really sad,

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.614
it covers all the emotional realms.

00:04:17.614 --> 00:04:20.240
- Yeah, that's why I had to do it.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.073
- [Kelly] I know, the character.

00:04:21.073 --> 00:04:22.475
You go all over the place.

00:04:22.475 --> 00:04:23.310
- Yeah.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.643
- Is that exhausting?

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.870
- No, 'cause it's so satisfying.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.162
- [Kelly] Okay, and it
breaks up the monotony.

00:04:29.162 --> 00:04:30.450
- And it's so much fun, you know.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.687
It's sort of like,

00:04:31.687 --> 00:04:33.560
